---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const APP = "https://login.form4dev.com";

const sections = [
  { id: "quickstart", title: "Quickstart" },
  { id: "html", title: "HTML form" },
  { id: "react", title: "React" },
  { id: "fetch", title: "fetch / curl" },
  { id: "magic-fields", title: "Magic fields" },
  { id: "captcha", title: "CAPTCHA" },
  { id: "webhooks", title: "Webhooks" },
  { id: "errors", title: "Error responses" },
];
---

<Base current="docs" title="Docs — Form4Dev">
  <div class="docs-shell container-wide">
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="side-eyebrow mono">/ docs</div>
      <nav>
        <ul>
          {sections.map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="content">
      <h1 class="display">Get a form working in 30 seconds.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Create a form in the dashboard, copy the endpoint URL, point an HTML
        <code>action=</code> at it. That's the whole quickstart.
      </p>

      <h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Sign up at <a href={`${APP}/register`}>{APP.replace('https://','')}/register</a> and verify your email.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Create form</strong>, name it, copy the endpoint URL — it looks like <code>https://login.form4dev.com/api/submit/&lt;slug&gt;</code>.</li>
        <li>Submit to it from anywhere. That's it.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="html">HTML form</h2>
      <pre class="code"><span class="t">&lt;form</span> <span class="a">action</span>=<span class="s">"https://login.form4dev.com/api/submit/contact"</span> <span class="a">method</span>=<span class="s">"POST"</span><span class="t">&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;input</span> <span class="a">name</span>=<span class="s">"email"</span> <span class="a">type</span>=<span class="s">"email"</span> <span class="a">required</span><span class="t">&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;textarea</span> <span class="a">name</span>=<span class="s">"message"</span> <span class="a">required</span><span class="t">&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;input</span> <span class="a">type</span>=<span class="s">"text"</span> <span class="a">name</span>=<span class="s">"_gotcha"</span> <span class="a">style</span>=<span class="s">"display:none"</span><span class="t">&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;button&gt;</span>Send<span class="t">&lt;/button&gt;</span>
<span class="t">&lt;/form&gt;</span></pre>
      <p class="muted-note"><strong><code>_gotcha</code></strong> is the honeypot — leave it empty in your real form, bots will fill it.</p>

      <h2 id="react">React</h2>
      <pre class="code"><span class="k">import</span> <span class="p">{`{`}</span> useForm, ValidationError <span class="p">{`}`}</span> <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">"@form4dev/react"</span><span class="p">;</span>

<span class="k">export function</span> <span class="fn">Contact</span><span class="p">() {`{`}</span>
  <span class="k">const</span> <span class="p">[</span>state, handleSubmit<span class="p">]</span> <span class="p">=</span> <span class="fn">useForm</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s">"contact"</span><span class="p">);</span>
  <span class="k">if</span> <span class="p">(</span>state.succeeded<span class="p">)</span> <span class="k">return</span> <span class="s">&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</span><span class="p">;</span>

  <span class="k">return</span> <span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="t">&lt;form onSubmit=</span><span class="p">{`{`}</span>handleSubmit<span class="p">{`}`}</span><span class="t">&gt;</span>
      <span class="t">&lt;input name="email" type="email" required/&gt;</span>
      <span class="t">&lt;ValidationError errors=</span><span class="p">{`{`}</span>state.errors<span class="p">{`}`}</span><span class="t"> field="email"/&gt;</span>
      <span class="t">&lt;button disabled=</span><span class="p">{`{`}</span>state.submitting<span class="p">{`}`}</span><span class="t">&gt;Send&lt;/button&gt;</span>
    <span class="t">&lt;/form&gt;</span>
  <span class="p">);</span>
<span class="p">{`}`}</span></pre>

      <h2 id="fetch">fetch / curl</h2>
      <pre class="code"><span class="k">curl</span> -X POST https://login.form4dev.com/api/submit/contact \
     -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
     -d <span class="s">'{`{`}"email":"ada@example.com","message":"hi"{`}`}'</span></pre>

      <h2 id="magic-fields">Magic fields</h2>
      <p>Drop these special fields into your payload and we'll route or label things automatically.</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>field</th><th>behavior</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>_replyto</code></td><td>Reply-To on the notification + autoresponder target.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>_subject</code></td><td>Overrides the notification subject.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>_cc</code> / <code>_bcc</code></td><td>Comma-separated extra recipients.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>_next</code></td><td>Override the success-redirect URL.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>_gotcha</code></td><td>Honeypot — leave blank. Filled = bot.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="captcha">CAPTCHA</h2>
      <p>An admin configures the provider once in system settings. Per-form, toggle <code>captchaRequired</code>. The submit endpoint accepts the token via the <code>X-Captcha-Token</code> header or the <code>_captcha</code> field. Supported: Cloudflare Turnstile, reCAPTCHA v2 + v3, hCaptcha.</p>

      <h2 id="webhooks">Webhooks</h2>
      <p>Add a webhook URL on the form's settings page. Every successful, non-spam submission POSTs the payload with an <code>X-Form4Dev-Signature</code> header (HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body, hex). Failed deliveries retry with exponential backoff for up to 5 attempts; the dashboard shows full delivery history.</p>

      <h2 id="errors">Error responses</h2>
      <p>Every error returns <code>{`{"error":{"code":"...","message":"...","fieldErrors"?:{},"retryAfter"?:N}}`}</code>.</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>status</th><th>code</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>400</code></td><td><code>VALIDATION_ERROR</code></td><td><code>error.fieldErrors</code> maps field id → list of messages.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td><code>AUTHENTICATION_ERROR</code></td><td>CAPTCHA token missing/rejected, or Bearer invalid.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>403</code></td><td><code>ORIGIN_NOT_ALLOWED</code></td><td>Submitting from a non-allowlisted origin.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>429</code></td><td><code>RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED</code></td><td>Per-IP, per-form, or org quota exceeded. <code>error.retryAfter</code> in seconds.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted-note">
        Building an AI agent integration? See <a href="/docs/agents">/docs/agents</a> — Bearer auth, cross-tenant guard, agent-skip-spam contract, and audit trail.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .docs-shell {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
    gap: 56px;
    padding: 64px 28px 96px;
  }
  .sidebar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 80px;
    align-self: start;
  }
  .side-eyebrow {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .sidebar nav ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .sidebar nav a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .sidebar nav a:hover {
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .content { max-width: 720px; }
  .content h1 { font-size: 44px; margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .content h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }
  .content .lede { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 600px; }
  .content p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content code {
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 0 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .content ol { line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 24px; }
  .content table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 14px 0;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .content th, .content td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 10px 12px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .content th {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .muted-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .code {
    background: var(--code-bg);
    color: var(--code-fg);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
    margin: 8px 0 14px;
  }
  .code .k { color: var(--code-key); }
  .code .s { color: var(--code-str); }
  .code .p { color: var(--code-pun); }
  .code .t { color: #6cd3ff; }
  .code .a { color: var(--accent); }
  .code .fn { color: #fff; font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .sidebar { position: static; }
  }
</style>
